{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1035316-evocations-for-claws-of-the-wood-dragon","id":1035316,"title":"Evocations for Claws of the Wood Dragon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-20T11:01:49-08:00","id":1035316,"title":"Evocations for Claws of the Wood Dragon?","content":"Has anyone made any/had any cool ideas for some?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T11:32:22-08:00","id":1035333,"title":"","content":"Nothing concrete, but go for poison. It's within the elemental purview of wood and powerful if used correctly. The first one can simply be a way to inflict Arrow Frog Venom on others, maybe consider expanding it to be able to inflict any mundane poison you've been infected with and survived, this will create an incentive to travel and find better poisons. The second evocation can be a bit more supernatural, instead of taking health or initiative, it takes motes. Draining essence from an opponent can be very powerful, but can be tweaking by simply adding or subtracting how much &quot;damage&quot; the poison does; 3m will half an opponents mote regen, 5m will stop it entirely, and any higher will cause the enemy to lose motes every turn. Because this is an evocation, you could say that it removes (Essence + 2) motes every turn, allowing it to become more powerful as your character does, and stay relevant against enemies with massive mote pools.<br /> <br /> The third and final evocation will simply be an extension of the second. Instead of draining motes, it drains Willpower. 1WP per turn is more than enough, and should be balanced by how many turns the poison stays in effect. Remember that even the strongest characters in the game will only have 10WP at most, so even losing one per turn ca quickly shut down how many times a character can use their most potent charms or sorceries.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that there are other good Evocations that one could come up with that focuses on the grappling ability of Bramble Hell Torment or that would synergize well with a particular Martial Art, but a Health&gt;Essence&gt;Willpower branch of poison evocations is a good a starting point as any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:46:18-08:00","id":1035386,"title":"","content":"Ones I was considering was &quot;Verdant World Claiming Branch&quot; which is a super stretchy arm allowing you to make Claw attacks one range band away.<br /> <br /> Fruits of the Dire Tree: An evocation which allows you to grow fruit in the palm of your hand. It can be nourishing fruits, as well as poisoned and hallucinatory fruits. The toxins can be extracted and applied to weapons or food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T12:55:18-08:00","id":1035390,"title":"","content":"I know that a number of people have suggested transferring Spring Razor's Evocations over entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T13:38:02-08:00","id":1035421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1035316-evocations-for-claws-of-the-wood-dragon?p=1035390#post1035390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that a number of people have suggested transferring Spring Razor's Evocations over entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I know a potentially horrible problem was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1024267-is-poison-a-viable-tactic-in-exalted-3rd-edition#post1024267\">revealed here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:44:12-08:00","id":1035516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1035316-evocations-for-claws-of-the-wood-dragon?p=1035421#post1035421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I know a potentially horrible problem was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1024267-is-poison-a-viable-tactic-in-exalted-3rd-edition#post1024267\">revealed here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black Claw Style says it's a totally unarmed style, so I wouldn't let you use Wood Dragon's Claw with it, regardless of what Vance says. I mean, I could see a specially designed very subtle set of Razor Claws with poison evocations designed to be used with Black Claw Style, but WDC is explicitly these huge bramble covered paws with rending talons on them.<br /> <br /> Tiger Style, Great. Ebon Shadow Style, sure. Black Claw Style, NO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:46:05-08:00","id":1035517,"title":"","content":"Yeah but its your own hand/claw. Saying it won't work with Black Claw Style is pretty much saying only humans can learn it, so demons need to have human hands to use it? Was Mara's hooves too much like weapons so she can't kick with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T00:26:28-08:00","id":1035650,"title":"","content":"Yeah... I drew inspiration for my character's Wood Dragon Claws evocations from the true form of Yumichika's zanpakuto, Ruri-iro Kujaku, from Bleach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/I03HPrhrLPA\" data-code=\"I03HPrhrLPA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/I03HPrhrLPA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:01:28-08:00","id":1037146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1035316-evocations-for-claws-of-the-wood-dragon?p=1035517#post1035517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but its your own hand/claw. Saying it won't work with Black Claw Style is pretty much saying only humans can learn it, so demons need to have human hands to use it? Was Mara's hooves too much like weapons so she can't kick with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they were meant to be treated as your own hands, they'd be written to be inherently compatible with all unarmed styles. They're not.<br /> <br /> As it is, WDC is compatible with any style using &quot;claw-type weapons or rending strikes&quot;. Some people think this makes it compatible with Black Claw because BC is stated to &quot;emphasize claw strikes&quot;. I disagree with this assessment, because &quot;claw strike&quot; is neither a claw-type weapon (as the style is unarmed-only), nor can it be really called &quot;rending&quot; when BC doesn't allow you to make lethal unarmed attacks.<br /> <br /> Then, of course, there's the matter of overall aesthetics. The entirety of Black Claw Style is predicated on playing an unwilling defender, a victim to an unprovoked assault. I can probably name a few things that would disturb that image more than turning your hands into steel-cutting murderclaws, but only a few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:54:21-08:00","id":1037375,"title":"","content":"Does it say specifically that WDC is a Weapon rather then Unarmed Natural Attack?<br /> <br /> There is nothing stopping you from using Tiger Style hand claw attack with Black Claw Style, its supernatural people will still feel it is self defense because it is a cagey evil demon martial art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:09:11-08:00","id":1037492,"title":"","content":"I want to figure out some Evocations for it following the line of Grass Sword from Adventure Time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T22:38:11-08:00","id":1037679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1035316-evocations-for-claws-of-the-wood-dragon?p=1037375#post1037375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it say specifically that WDC is a Weapon rather then Unarmed Natural Attack?<br /> <br /> There is nothing stopping you from using Tiger Style hand claw attack with Black Claw Style, its supernatural people will still feel it is self defense because it is a cagey evil demon martial art.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was an unarmed natural attack, you could use it with every MA style (well, practically every MA style). Given that it has the stats of a light artifact weapon, I'd treat it as one.<br /> <br /> But, honestly, even if the rules specifically said &quot;Wood Dragon's Claw can be used with Black Claw Style,&quot; which they don't, I STILL wouldn't allow it, because, as Morangias notes, it breaks the aesthetic of the style something fierce. So, yeah, I wouldn't let a Blood Ape practice it either, regardless of what weapons they were carrying. At the very least, I don't think it would work on humans, not unless the Blood Ape had figured out how to turn into a nonthreatening form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}